Package: com.example.multifloat
Name: MultiFloat
Version: 0.5.0
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64e
Description: Multi-floating window / split-view tweak for iOS 17 (roothide / arm64e). 0.5.0 fixes a config footgun that made 0.4.0 show NOTHING on device: the master switch 'enabled' defaulted to false, so changing 'hostEnabled' alone left the tweak fully inert. 0.5.0 (a) defaults enabled=true so the shell window appears on install (0.3.0 proved the shell alone is stable), (b) auto-repairs a self-contradictory config (enabled=false while hostEnabled=true) at launch and rewrites it, (c) spells out in the log that enabled is the master switch and hostEnabled only gates real hosting. Hosting chain S1..S7 unchanged from 0.4.0: user-triggered only, crash-guard marker makes a crash loop impossible, step-by-step attribution via /var/mobile/MF-host-step.txt, and the FBScene -activateWithTransitionContext:nil call is still removed. No hooks are installed. Log: /var/mobile/MultiFloat.log
Maintainer: QingC12 <QingC12@users.noreply.github.com>
Author: QingC12
Section: Tweaks
Depends: firmware (>= 15.0)
